  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "41999870",
      "title": "Creating a NextJS Project",
      "sourceHash": "6d3736325dbd51af0cc2300d38ee1bb9f374108d26a37c4a2d11ec78783fa443",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.51,
          "end": 1.98,
          "en": "So therefore,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 1.98,
          "end": 4.89,
          "en": "now that we know what NextJS is,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 4.89,
          "end": 6.3,
          "en": "let's see it in action",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 6.3,
          "end": 9.81,
          "en": "and let's create a new NextJS project.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 9.81,
          "end": 12.51,
          "en": "And we do that in a slightly different way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 12.51,
          "end": 16.14,
          "en": "than we did it for standard React projects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 16.14,
          "end": 17.4,
          "en": "because we need a project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 17.4,
          "end": 19.77,
          "en": "that comes with NextJS pre-installed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 19.77,
          "end": 22.53,
          "en": "and that has a certain structure and setup",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 22.53,
          "end": 25.11,
          "en": "that's needed by NextJS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 25.11,
          "end": 27.483,
          "en": "And you'll see what I mean in just a second.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 28.32,
          "end": 32.85,
          "en": "You can visit nextjs.org to find setup instructions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 32.85,
          "end": 36.93,
          "en": "And there, you should somewhere see a command like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 36.93,
          "end": 40.08,
          "en": "npx create-next-app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 40.08,
          "end": 44.46,
          "en": "which can be executed to create a new Next project.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 44.46,
          "end": 47.7,
          "en": "And it's therefore this command which I will execute.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 47.7,
          "end": 50.7,
          "en": "Therefore, I opened up my terminal on Windows.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 50.7,
          "end": 52.41,
          "en": "It's simply the command prompt.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 52.41,
          "end": 54.66,
          "en": "And you can paste in that command here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 54.66,
          "end": 57.09,
          "en": "And then thereafter add a white space,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 57.09,
          "end": 59.91,
          "en": "and then any project name of your choice,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 59.91,
          "end": 64.593,
          "en": "like first-next-app or something like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 65.76,
          "end": 68.58,
          "en": "And this will then go ahead and create a new folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 68.58,
          "end": 70.77,
          "en": "and a new Next project in that folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 70.77,
          "end": 74.19,
          "en": "though, first, it'll ask you a couple of questions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 74.19,
          "end": 76.86,
          "en": "For example, whether you wanna use TypeScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 76.86,
          "end": 79.14,
          "en": "And whilst TypeScript is amazing,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 79.14,
          "end": 81.09,
          "en": "not every student knows it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 81.09,
          "end": 83.7,
          "en": "And therefore, in this course, I'll not use it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 83.7,
          "end": 86.13,
          "en": "I will check ESLint though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 86.13,
          "end": 89.16,
          "en": "We could use Tailwind CSS for styling",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 89.16,
          "end": 91.11,
          "en": "and amazing CSS library,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 91.11,
          "end": 94.14,
          "en": "but since this course here is not about styling",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 94.14,
          "end": 95.7,
          "en": "and not about Tailwind,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 95.7,
          "end": 98.16,
          "en": "and I therefore wanna keep the amount",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 98.16,
          "end": 101.49000000000001,
          "en": "of styling related code we have to write to a minimum,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 101.49000000000001,
          "end": 103.25999999999999,
          "en": "I'll choose no here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 103.25999999999999,
          "end": 106.22999999999999,
          "en": "You could opt for an alternative project structure,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 106.22999999999999,
          "end": 107.28,
          "en": "which we don't need,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 107.28,
          "end": 111.72,
          "en": "but you should confirm the App Router if asked.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 111.72,
          "end": 113.703,
          "en": "So you should pick yes here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 115.02000000000001,
          "end": 117.03,
          "en": "Now, last but not least, I'll choose no",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 117.03,
          "end": 118.65,
          "en": "for this alias question.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 118.65,
          "end": 122.31,
          "en": "And with that, finally, the project is being created,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 122.31,
          "end": 124.38,
          "en": "the dependencies are being installed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 124.38,
          "end": 127.953,
          "en": "And we'll soon have a NextJS project in which we can work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 130.77,
          "end": 134.88,
          "en": "Now, I did open up that project in Visual Studio Code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 134.88,
          "end": 137.97,
          "en": "Obviously, you can use any code editor of your choice,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 137.97,
          "end": 141.24,
          "en": "and I actually opened a slightly edited version",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 141.24,
          "end": 144.93,
          "en": "of this default project that's being created.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 144.93,
          "end": 147.51,
          "en": "It's the same structure essentially,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 147.51,
          "end": 151.89,
          "en": "but I replaced the content of this app folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 151.89,
          "end": 155.28,
          "en": "And this app folder is there right from the start,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 155.28,
          "end": 157.23,
          "en": "even in an unedited project.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 157.23,
          "end": 160.2,
          "en": "But I replace the files that are in that folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 160.2,
          "end": 161.97,
          "en": "with new files.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 161.97,
          "end": 165.45,
          "en": "And attached, you find my updated starting snapshot,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 165.45,
          "end": 169.59,
          "en": "also a CodeSandbox version, so that you can follow along",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 169.59,
          "end": 172.05,
          "en": "without installing anything locally",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 172.05,
          "end": 176.55,
          "en": "so that you can use that exact same starting state as I do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 176.55,
          "end": 179.46,
          "en": "It is enough if you replace your app folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 179.46,
          "end": 183.66,
          "en": "and your public folder since I also added an image in there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 183.66,
          "end": 186.54,
          "en": "As well as your eslintrc.json fall",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 186.54,
          "end": 189.3,
          "en": "since I added one rule in there with mine.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 189.3,
          "end": 191.283,
          "en": "The other files are the same.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 193.02,
          "end": 196.77,
          "en": "And with that, you can then go into your terminal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 196.77,
          "end": 197.94,
          "en": "in that project.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 197.94,
          "end": 200.79,
          "en": "So open your default terminal or command prompt",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 200.79,
          "end": 203.16,
          "en": "and navigate into this project,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 203.16,
          "end": 206.52,
          "en": "or use the one integrated into Visual Studio Code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 206.52,
          "end": 210.45,
          "en": "which is navigated into that project automatically.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 210.45,
          "end": 213.63,
          "en": "And make sure that you run NPM installed once",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 213.63,
          "end": 216.9,
          "en": "to ensure that all dependencies are installed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 216.9,
          "end": 220.26,
          "en": "On CodeSandbox, you don't need to do that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 220.26,
          "end": 222.32999999999998,
          "en": "And thereafter, run npm run dev",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 222.32999999999998,
          "end": 224.19,
          "en": "to start the development server,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 224.19,
          "end": 227.67000000000002,
          "en": "which allows you to preview the application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 227.67000000000002,
          "end": 230.34,
          "en": "On CodeSandbox, you also don't need to do that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 230.34,
          "end": 233.223,
          "en": "since there, the server is already up and running.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 234.69,
          "end": 236.88,
          "en": "Now with that, you then see the address,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 236.88,
          "end": 240.09,
          "en": "which you can visit to preview the project.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 240.09,
          "end": 242.01,
          "en": "And if you then go to that address,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 242.01,
          "end": 244.71,
          "en": "you should see something like this on the screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 244.71,
          "end": 248.16,
          "en": "And that's that very basic first starting project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 248.16,
          "end": 250.41,
          "en": "I prepared for you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 250.41,
          "end": 253.74,
          "en": "And now we can take a closer look at that folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 253.74,
          "end": 255.123,
          "en": "and how that all works.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
